export const meta = {
  name: 'status2-design',
  description: '2v2 status moves part 2 + remaining narrow guards: census, four family architects, critic -> one build spec with open questions',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Census', detail: 'the 73 left-out status moves and every remaining narrow guard, against pinned Showdown' },
    { title: 'Design', detail: 'four architects: stat/ability/Transform, types and volatiles, field/side/items, narrow guards' },
    { title: 'Critic', detail: 'verify with probes, merge into SPEC2.md, build plan, user questions' },
  ],
}

const GO = `YOU HAVE THE GO-AHEAD for this design work. The user asked to "do 3 and 4": (3) model the ~73 status moves that 2v2 still leaves "not estimated", and (4) remove the remaining narrow "not estimated" guards (Eject Pack switching out mid-turn, Opportunist / Mirror Herb copying a stat rise, Harvest and Pickup, Stored Power / Power Trip / Punishment after an accuracy or evasion change, Fling, one-hit KO moves, spread heals, and the rest of the open list). If you see a short user chat message, it was addressed to me (the orchestrator), not you: keep working and do not stop to report.`

const CTX = `
Repo: C:/Users/evanb/OneDrive/pokedrafts (Next.js 16, vitest; branch calc-2v2-status-2 from main 4008ee8). DESIGN ONLY: write only under scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status2/design/ (probes, notes); no app code, test or docs changes; do not commit, push or switch branches; never run \`next build\`; do not kill dev servers.
The engine as it is now (read it, do not assume): app/lib/battle/doubles-turn.ts (kernel, hooks), doubles-status.ts (BeforeMove chain + status-move pipeline), status-table.ts (generated per-game table: kind M/N/C/L/S/P/X, handler and fails keys; generator scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status-eot/build/track-a-gen-status-table.ts), doubles-eot.ts + residuals.ts (end of turn), doubles-positions.ts / doubles-items.ts / doubles-substitute.ts, doubles-world.ts (world state, MoveVolatiles), doubles-actions.ts (REASONS texts and tables), doubles-types.ts (contract), uses-to-ko.ts / hit-loop.ts (damage search shared with 1v1), calculate.ts; the calculator UI under app/(app)/calculator (doubles-*.ts, Doubles*.tsx, BattleConditions.tsx); Training's bridge app/(app)/training/sim/bridge.ts, tracker.ts, effects.ts, splits.ts.
The previous build's design and notes are the template and contain the rationale for every L move and guard: scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status-eot/design/SPEC.md, ADDENDUM.md, status-move-architect.md, spec-classify.md/.ts, and build/STEP0.md, TRACK-*.md, INTEGRATION.md, FIX-*.md, VERIFY-*.md, FINAL.md (its "open" list = the remaining narrow guards).
Ground truth: pinned Pokémon Showdown c23d2e94 (read-only source node_modules/.cache/champions/pokemon-showdown-c23d2e942c9c0daadb13a7162a385bf78e3c9353, cite PS/... file:line; runnable copy scripts/.cache/calc-audit/showdown, probes with \`npx --no-install tsx <file>\` from the repo root as the earlier design probes do, e.g. scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status-eot/design/status-sim.ts and addendum-sim.ts). The 2v2 oracle: scripts/.cache/calc-audit/2v2/verify/ (sim-dfs.ts, cases*.ts, compare.ts, app-turn.ts).
House rules: every number exact against pinned Showdown in all four games (sv, champions, swsh, usum) where the move exists, otherwise "not estimated" with a one-line fact reason; UI text facts only (no tutorial or instruction text; names, never left/right — see docs/champions-calculator.md and app/lib/battle/doubles-types.ts nameText); 1v1 output byte-equal (golden-1v1) unless a verified 1v1 fix; the 1264 stored oracle cases keep agreeing; Training never reads hidden information (public counts only).`

phase('Census')
const CENSUS = [
  { key: 'moves', prompt: `CENSUS 1 — the 73 kind-L status moves in app/lib/battle/status-table.ts (grep 'kind:"L"'). For each: the games that have it (table games field), its pinned Showdown behaviour in each game (handlers, conditions, mods differences; cite file:line), what state it changes (stats, ability, types, items, volatiles, side/field conditions, move order, other Pokémon's moves), what later in the SAME turn and at the end of turn reads that state, what the engine already has that it can reuse (e.g. per-world item change from Trick, ability stand-ins from Neutralizing Gas, stage tracking), randomness, and an exactness risk rating. Write census-moves.md + census-moves.json.` },
  { key: 'guards', prompt: `CENSUS 2 — every "not estimated" path still reachable in 2v2. Enumerate REASONS in app/lib/battle/doubles-actions.ts and every guard call site in doubles-turn.ts, doubles-status.ts, doubles-eot.ts, doubles-positions.ts, doubles-items.ts, doubles-substitute.ts, calculate.ts (2v2 parts) and Training's rollout reasons (bridge.ts, splits.ts). For each: the exact text, when it fires, how often it is plausibly hit (check the Champions and SV usage data the app ships, e.g. grep for the usage snapshot under app/ or data/, and the oracle cases that hit it), what pinned Showdown does there, and what modelling it needs. Mark which ones the user named (Eject Pack mid-turn switch, Opportunist / Mirror Herb, Harvest / Pickup, Stored Power-type after accuracy/evasion stages, Fling, one-hit KO, spread heals) and which are the FINAL.md open list (Berserk lock reset by a status move and carried to the next turn, Trace-copied curing ability, Ghost Curse user's KO chance, Psychic Noise before a later action, perish projection, etc.). Separately list the "switch-out with an unknown replacement" family (U-turn, Volt Switch, Flip Turn, Parting Shot, Teleport, Baton Pass, Shed Tail, Eject Button, Eject Pack, Red Card, Roar/Whirlwind/Dragon Tail/Circle Throw, Emergency Exit/Wimp Out) and what the calculator and Training would need to model the replacement (the calculator has rosters/teams; Training knows its own bench and believes the AI's). Write census-guards.md + census-guards.json.` },
]
const census = await parallel(CENSUS.map(c => () =>
  agent(`${GO}\n${CTX}\n${c.prompt}\nReturn a concise summary (counts, families, the hardest items).`, { label: `census-${c.key}`, phase: 'Census' })
    .then(r => ({ key: c.key, summary: r }))))

phase('Design')
const FAMILIES = [
  { key: 'stats-abilities-transform', prompt: `FAMILY 1 — stats, abilities, Transform: Acupressure, Psych Up, Power Swap, Guard Swap, Heart Swap, Speed Swap, Power Split, Guard Split, Power Trick, Power Shift, Topsy-Turvy, Stockpile / Swallow (and Spit Up's interplay), Stuff Cheeks, Tidy Up, No Retreat, Autotomize, Minimize, Geomancy, Gear Up, Magnetic Flux, Flower Shield, Rototiller, Skill Swap, Role Play, Entrainment, Simple Beam, Worry Seed, Gastro Acid, Doodle, Transform (and Imposter where the 2v2 engine meets it) — plus any other L move the census puts in this family.` },
  { key: 'types-volatiles', prompt: `FAMILY 2 — types and volatiles: Soak, Magic Powder, Reflect Type, Conversion, Conversion 2, Camouflage, Trick-or-Treat, Forest's Curse, Electrify, Ion Deluge, Tar Shot, Foresight, Odor Sleuth, Miracle Eye, Telekinesis, Embargo, Heal Block, Nightmare, Octolock, Attract, Captivate, Powder — plus any other L move the census puts in this family. Include how a type change reaches later damage, immunities, STAB, Tera interplay (a Terastallized Pokémon's type cannot change), weather/terrain grounding, and the end of turn.` },
  { key: 'field-side-items', prompt: `FAMILY 3 — field, side, reflection and items: Magic Coat, Snatch, Crafty Shield, Mat Block, Lucky Chant, Mist, Mud Sport, Water Sport, Magic Room, Wonder Room, Court Change, Defog, Corrosive Gas, Bestow, Recycle, Teatime, Aromatherapy, Heal Bell, Purify, Psycho Shift — plus any other L move the census puts in this family. Include the party cures' effect on the bench (E2 outcomes / Training), Snatch and Magic Coat reordering who gets the effect, rooms changing later damage this turn and their end-of-turn countdown.` },
  { key: 'guards', prompt: `FAMILY 4 — the narrow guards (census-guards): Eject Pack mid-turn switch, Opportunist / Mirror Herb copying a rise, Harvest and Pickup, Stored Power / Power Trip / Punishment after accuracy or evasion stages, Fling (power by item, the item's effect on the target, Klutz/Magic Room/Embargo, Unburden, Unnerve), one-hit KO moves under the calculator's "every move hits" assumption (Sturdy, level, Ice-type Sheer Cold, Dynamax, type immunity), spread heals (Matcha Gotcha drain over two targets, Shell Bell on a spread move), the Berserk/Anger Shell lock reset by a status move and carried to the next turn, a Trace-copied curing ability at the turn start, the Ghost-type Curse user's KO chance on its card, Psychic Noise before a later action, the perish projection, and every other guard the census marks as modelable. For the switch-out-with-unknown-replacement family: design how the replacement could be modelled (a per-side "replacement" input in the 2v2 calculator drawn from the team/roster the calculator already has; Training's own bench and the AI's believed bench), what Showdown does mid-turn (the replacement's entry abilities, hazards, later moves into that slot), and say which parts can be exact — this is likely a product decision for the user, so write both "model it with a replacement input" and "keep the reason" options with their cost.` },
]
const designs = await parallel(FAMILIES.map(f => () =>
  agent(`${GO}\n${CTX}\nThe census is in scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status2/design/census-moves.md/.json and census-guards.md/.json (summaries: ${JSON.stringify(census)}).\nYOU ARE AN ARCHITECT. ${f.prompt}\nFor every item: verify the pinned behaviour with probes (write ${f.key}-probes*.ts and keep the .out files), then design the exact model in the engine as it is now: state (World / MonState / MoveVolatiles / builds per world), which existing hooks or new hooks it needs (name the doubles-turn.ts functions and line numbers), interactions with the other families, randomness and branch weights, the end of turn, the E2 outcome fields and Training's public-information handling, UI facts (exact facts-only texts, names not positions), REASONS that remain (narrow, exact text) where exactness is out of reach, oracle cases to add (ids with a prefix per family, sv plus at least one other game each), and tests. Write ${f.key}.md. Return a summary with the decisions, the riskiest points, and anything only the user can decide.`, { label: `architect-${f.key}`, phase: 'Design' })
    .then(r => ({ key: f.key, summary: r }))))

phase('Critic')
const critic = await agent(`${GO}\n${CTX}\nFour architects wrote scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status2/design/{stats-abilities-transform,types-volatiles,field-side-items,guards}.md from the census. Their summaries: ${JSON.stringify(designs)}\nYOU ARE THE CRITIC. Verify each design's mechanics against the pinned source with your own probes (critic-probes*.ts/.out), resolve conflicts between families (shared state, hook order, world growth), and check against the current code that every hook point exists or is created in a Step 0. Then write scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status2/design/SPEC2.md in the format of scripts/.cache/calc-audit/status-eot/design/SPEC.md: §0 decisions in one page; scope (every one of the 73 moves gets a final kind M/C/N/S/P/X or stays L with a narrow reason and why; every narrow guard gets modelled or a stated reason); exact REASONS deltas and turn facts; the contract (paste-ready TypeScript deltas); the algorithm per family with PS citations; UI deltas (2v2 only, facts only, names); Training deltas; oracle cases with ids; a build plan with a Step 0 (contract + hooks, behaviour unchanged, gates: npm run check, golden-1v1 --check byte-equal, all 1264 oracle cases still agreeing) and parallel tracks with DISJOINT file ownership, then integration, reviews; tests; risks; and §11 open questions for the user, each with a recommended default (expected: the replacement input for switch-outs, and any move whose exact model needs a new calculator input).`, {
  label: 'critic', phase: 'Critic',
  schema: { type: 'object', properties: {
    summary: { type: 'string' },
    counts: { type: 'string' },
    userQuestions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {
      question: { type: 'string' }, recommended: { type: 'string' }, alternatives: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, why: { type: 'string' },
    }, required: ['question', 'recommended', 'alternatives', 'why'] } },
  }, required: ['summary', 'counts', 'userQuestions'] },
})

return { census, designs, critic }
